          "name": "GeneralizedStafford.FilteredAlgebraData.gr_succ_eq_zero_iff"
        },
        {
          "file": "GeneralizedStafford/Setting.lean",
          "name": "GeneralizedStafford.FilteredAlgebraData.gr_mul"
        }
      ],
      "depends_on": [],
      "notes": "The ten fields encode the actual nonnegative associated graded: gr_n:F_n→G_n is linear and onto; ker gr_0=0; ker gr_(n+1)=F_n; multiplication is respected. The graded-algebra instance makes G the direct sum of the G_n. The data have 1∈F_0, not F_0=k, and no finite-dimensional-piece field. The theorem separately assumes Infinite k, IsSimpleRing U, IsDomain/IsNoetherianRing G and finite Krull dimension. Semantic equivalence to an actual associated graded uses these exact kernel/surjection/multiplication conditions, not a freely chosen symbol algebra."
    },
